>> title: Peach Cobbler
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: peach, dessert, baked, biscuit, southern
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: cobbler, peach cobbler, deep dish peach cobbler, dropped biscuit cobbler
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> pairs-with: banana-pudding, sweet-potato-pie, french-vanilla-ice-cream
>> step.1: Bake the fruit twenty minutes before the topping goes anywhere near it. Dropped onto raw peaches the biscuit sits in cold juice and comes out doughy underneath, which is the one way this dessert goes wrong.
>> step.2: toss the fruit
>> step.3: bake the fruit alone 375°F 20 min
>> step.4: whisk the dry
>> step.5: cut the butter in, cream to a shaggy dough
>> step.6: spoon the dough on, bake 375°F 35 min

Bake the fruit twenty minutes before the topping goes anywhere near it. Dropped onto raw peaches the biscuit sits in cold juice and comes out doughy underneath, which is the one way this dessert goes wrong.

Toss @ripe peaches{3%lb}(1.4 kg; peeled and sliced thick), @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g), @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(16 g), @lemon juice{2%Tbs}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, @fine sea salt{1/4%tsp}.

Bake @&(~1)sugared peaches{} in a #9x13-in baking dish{} at 375°F (190°C) for ~bake{20%min}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1 1/2%cup}(195 g), @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @baking powder{2%tsp}(8 g), @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}.

Cut @&(~1)dry mixture{} together with @cold unsalted butter{6%Tbs}(85 g; cubed), @heavy cream{3/4%cup}(180 mL) to a shaggy dough.

Bake @&(~3)hot peaches{} under spoonfuls of @&(~1)biscuit dough{}, scattered with @demerara sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), at 375°F (190°C) for ~bake{35%min}.

Cool it half an hour before it is spooned out. Straight from the oven the juice is thin and runs off the plate, and it thickens as it settles.
